# Review

## Summary

The only framework-like structure in the note is the bulleted taxonomy of five valuation lenses in Current answer. The note contains no table, notation or equation.

One sentence could not replace the taxonomy without losing meaningful information. The lenses are discriminative. They apply at different times: admission, writing, live use and ranking at scale. They rely on different evidence: the contract, the reader's prior, counterfactual withholding and structural metadata. Each one also routes to a different grounding note, so the taxonomy supports repeated lookup. Later inferences use the distinctions. The cold-start problem depends on the fact that two lenses are observable only after retention. The asymmetric-pressure problem depends on separating validity from value.

The lens list does not add vocabulary that the argument later leaves unused, so the taxonomy is not decorative.
